 of aerosols\nusing RADAER logical, public :: l_ntpreq_n_activ_sum True to include total number concentration of active aerosol in\nnon-transported prognostics (e.g. for combination with an external cloud\nmask for calculating CDNC in the UM hybrid resolution model) logical, public :: l_ntpreq_dryd_nuc_sol True to include to include the dry diameter for nucleation soluble mode logical, public :: l_ukca_sfix True for diagnosing UKCA CCN at fixed supersaturation logical, public :: l_fix_neg_pvol_wat True to check, trap and fix for negative values in 'pvol' and 'mdwat' logical, public :: l_fix_ukca_impscav True to fix impaction scavenging bugs logical, public :: l_fix_nacl_density True to correct sea-salt density logical, public :: l_improve_aero_drydep if True the surface type used by the aerosol dry deposition is provided\nby the parent, rather than being inferred from roughness length in\nGLOMAP. logical, public :: l_fix_ukca_water_content True to fix bugs in the calculation of aerosol water content values. logical, public :: l_fix_ukca_activate_pdf True to fix probability density fn. of updraft velocities in Activate logical, public :: l_fix_ukca_activate_vert_rep True to fix CDNC vertical replication bug in Activate logical, public :: l_bug_repro_tke_index True to reproduce effects of an old bug in the calculation of updraft\npdf spread related to TKE indexing in the Unified Model logical, public :: l_fix_ukca_hygroscopicities True to update aerosol component hygroscopicities to kappa-Kohler values\nand fix bug in calculation of volume-weighted hygroscopicity value logical, public :: l_dust_mp_ageing True for dust and microplastics being subjected to nuc scav, conden,\ncoag, ageing, and activation logical, public :: l_skip_const_setup Control argument for skipping set up of constants if already done logical, public :: l_cloud_pc2 True if the atmosphere model is using the PC2 cloud scheme logical, public :: l_strat_chem True if UKCA is using a scheme that involves stratospheric chemistry\ni.e. Std Strat, Strattrop or CRI-strat logical, public :: l_offline_photol True to read photolysis rates from offline_photol_rates_file, rather\nthan calculating them online character(len=256), public :: offline_photol_rates_file path to offline photolysis rates file character(len=256), public :: environment_data_file path to environment namelist file character(len=256), public :: initial_tracer_file path to initial tracer file character(len=256), public :: initial_ntp_file path to initial non-transported prognostics (NTP) file character(len=256), public :: output_dir directory for output files, relative to the working directory (empty\nmeans the working directory) Functions public  function output_file_path (cfg, filename) result(path) Return the path to write an output file to: the file name inside the\nconfigured output directory. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( box_config_type ), intent(in) :: cfg The box model configuration character(len=*), intent(in) :: filename Name of the output file Return Value character(len=512) Path to write the output file to Subroutines public  subroutine read_box_config (filename, cfg) Reads the box model configuration from a user-provided namelist file and\nstores the configuration in a box_config_type type. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: filename Name of the namelist file to read type( box_config_type ), intent(out) :: cfg The resulting box model configuration read from the namelist file public  subroutine print_box_config (cfg) Print the box model configuration to the log, grouped by namelist\nsection. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( box_config_type ), intent(in) :: cfg The box model configuration to print","tags":"","url":"module/box_config_mod.html"},{"title":"box_shell_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Module holding the box model driver: it reads the box config and inputs,\nsets up UKCA, then runs UKCA for each time step and writes the output. Uses umprintmgr ereport_mod Subroutines public  subroutine box_shell (namelist_path) Run the box model: read the box config namelist and the input files it\nnames, set up UKCA and photolysis, then step UKCA through the model\nduration and write the tracer output. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: namelist_path Path to the box config namelist, which names the other input files","tags":"","url":"module/box_shell_mod.html"},{"title":"UM_ParCore – UKCA Box Model","text":"Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: mype = 0 integer, public :: nproc = 1 integer, public :: nproc_max = 1","tags":"","url":"module/um_parcore.html"},{"title":"box_internal_ukca_config_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Module for setting up UKCA's internal configuration from the box config\n(setup_internal_ukca_config, which calls ukca_setup), and for storing\ninternal ukca configuration options that are dependent on configuration\nchoices, but also need to be made accessible by the box model. Note these values are only valid after ukca_setup() has been called, and\nthe internal configuration been set up. This includes the number of photolytic reactions, which is needed by the\nbox model to allocate arrays for photolysis rates. Uses ukca_missing_data_mod Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, protected :: n_dust_emissions = imdi Number of dust emission size ranges integer, protected :: jppj = imdi Number of photolytic reactions Subroutines public  subroutine setup_internal_ukca_config (cfg) Set up UKCA's internal configuration by calling ukca_setup with the box\nconfig, the box model's fixed settings (box_const_mod) and the JULES\nsurface type indices. setup_jules must be called first. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( box_config_type ), intent(in) :: cfg The box model configuration public  subroutine read_internal_ukca_config () Get the ukca internal options needed by the box model. Must be called\nafter ukca_setup() has been called. Arguments None","tags":"","url":"module/box_internal_ukca_config_mod.html"},{"title":"fastjx_inphot_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Subroutines public  subroutine fastjx_inphot () Arguments None","tags":"","url":"module/fastjx_inphot_mod.html"},{"title":"planet_constants_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real, public, parameter :: planet_radius = 6371229.0","tags":"","url":"module/planet_constants_mod.html"},{"title":"box_config_validator_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Module for validating the configuration of the UKCA box model. Uses ukca_api_mod box_err_codes_mod ereport_mod Subroutines public  subroutine validate_config (cfg) Validate the inputted configuration Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( box_config_type ), intent(in) :: cfg The configuration to validate","tags":"","url":"module/box_config_validator_mod.html"},{"title":"missing_data_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real, public, parameter :: rmdi_pp = -1.0e+30 real, public, parameter :: rmdi_old = -32768.0 real, public, parameter :: rmdi = -32768.0*32768.0 integer, public, parameter :: imdi = -32768","tags":"","url":"module/missing_data_mod.html"},{"title":"box_socrates_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Module for storing constants for the UKCA box model that are stored in\nthe socrates model for the operational runs. To reduce the number of\ndependencies on socrates, we store the constants here in the box model\nand set them to the same values as in socrates. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: ip_aerosol_param_moist = 2 Parametrization for moist aerosols integer, public, parameter :: ip_accum_sulphate = 10 Aerosols for the sulphur cycle - Accumulation mode sulphate integer, public, parameter :: ip_aitken_sulphate = 11 Aitken mode sulphate","tags":"","url":"module/box_socrates_mod.html"},{"title":"box_environment_mod – UKCA Box Model","text":"Module to handle the creation of the box model environment, stored in\nbox_environment_type. This holds all environmental fields for a box model\nrun. The API call ukca_set_environment is then used to pass this\ninformation from the box model into the main UKCA model. Uses box_const_mod umprintmgr ukca_missing_data_mod ieee_arithmetic box_debug_mod box_jules_mod ukca_api_mod ereport_mod box_internal_ukca_config_mod Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=*), public, parameter :: mod_name = \"box_environment_mod\" Module name for logging and error reporting Interfaces public        interface print_field private  subroutine print_field_real(label, value, fmt) Print a labelled real value, with missing data shown as NaN Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label The label to print before the value real, intent(in) :: value The value to print character(len=*), intent(in) :: fmt The format to print the label and value with private  subroutine print_field_int(label, value, fmt) Print a labelled integer value, with missing data shown as NaN Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label The label to print before the value integer, intent(in) :: value The value to print character(len=*), intent(in) :: fmt The format to print the label and value with private  subroutine print_field_logical(label, value, fmt) Print a labelled logical value Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label The label to print before the value logical, intent(in) :: value The value to print character(len=*), intent(in) :: fmt The format to print the label and value with Derived Types type, public :: box_environment_type derived type for storing all ukca environmental fields Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real, public :: z_top_of_model = rmdi height of model top (m) real, public :: sin_d